WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.120
Netflix is always adding top-notch movies
to its library, but it's also constantly taking

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:05.980
options away.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.280
Here are the movies you have to watch before
they leave Netflix in November 2019.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.060
Until November 1, you can dine in hell alongside
Gerard Butler's King Leonidas by watching

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:17.920
the 2006 action film 300.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:23.500
Directed by Zack Snyder, 300 is based on Frank
Miller's comic book series of the same name,

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.140
which offers a fictionalized retelling of
the real-life Battle of Thermopylae that occurred

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:30.280
in 480 BC during the Greco-Persian Wars.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:35.239
Butler top-lines the film as Leonidas, leader
of the Grecian city-state Sparta, who takes

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:40.320
300 Spartans into battle against the king
of Persia, Xerxes, and his 300,000 soldiers.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:44.409
This is a flick filled with violence, action,
and bloodshed, and is sure to please anyone

00:00:44.409 --> 00:00:48.440
keen on watching Gerard Butler swing around
a sword and kick his enemy into a pit.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.420
"This is Sparta"

00:00:55.719 --> 00:01:00.709
The original 1980 sports comedy film, Caddyshack
stars Chevy Chase as Ty Webb, a golfer at

00:01:00.709 --> 00:01:01.900
Bushwood Country Club.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:06.270
The elite establishment, which Ty's father
co-founded, gets a rude awakening when the

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:10.720
loud-mouthed, new-money golfer Al, played
by Rodney Dangerfield, takes the green.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:15.360
Bushwood is also dealing with a seemingly
never-ending war between an evil gopher bent

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.460
on destroying the golf course and Bushwood's
groundskeeper Carl Spackler, who's intent

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:20.840
on exterminating the rodent.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.280
Like its predecessor, Caddyshack II is also
available to stream on Netflix until November

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:25.800
1.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:30.700
Clint Eastwood's 2008 drama Gran Torino is
a movie you certainly won't want to miss before

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.700
it leaves Netflix.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:36.219
While you might know Eastwood from his time
in Westerns, Gran Torino sees the actor tackling

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:37.140
modern drama.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:41.540
The venerated actor directs, produces, and
stars in Gran Torino, a film about a widowed

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:44.880
Korean War vet who forms a unique relationship
with his neighbor, Thao.

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:49.340
Critics have held Gran Torino in high esteem,
so if you've yet to see it for yourself, you

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:51.540
have until November 1 to learn why.

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:56.840
Until November 1, subscribers can stream Groundhog
Day, which follows Phil Connors as he relives

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.180
February 2, 1992 over and over again.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:05.119
As he does, he slowly learns to respect others,
open up his heart, and even save another person

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:05.620
from death.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:09.680
Easily one of Bill Murray's best films, you
might not get another chance to see the film

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.000
on Netflix again soon.

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:14.980
It's sweet, it's inventive, it spawned a whole
new meaning for the term "groundhog day,"

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:17.680
and it's on Netflix for only a few more days.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:18.560
"I'm sorry?

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:19.720
What was that again?"

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:21.120
"I'm a god?"

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:22.160
"You're god?"

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.240
"I'm a god, not the god.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:26.260
I don’t think."

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:30.540
The Scream franchise and the Scary Movie series
go together like peanut butter and jelly:

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.080
it's hard to have one without the other.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:36.500
Netflix subscribers can sit down for a double
feature like no other by watching Wes Craven's

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:40.890
iconic slasher flick Scream, which centers
around high school student Sidney Prescott

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.460
and the masked murderer who's stalking her
and her friends.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:48.230
Then you can immediately follow it up with
Scary Movie 2, a spoof on supernatural horror

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:51.580
movies that covers everything from The Exorcist
to The Amityville Horror.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.620
Both flicks will stick around Netflix until
November 1.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.080
After you've thoroughly satisfied yourself
with Halloween candy, retire to your couch

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.900
for a six-hour binging marathon.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:05.200
Until November 1, Netflix subscribers can
stream The Lord of the Rings: The Two Towers

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.930
and The Lord of the Rings: The Return of the
King, the final two installments of the Lord

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:10.060
of the Rings trilogy.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:14.580
Follow the trials and tribulations of the
fellowship as they reunite with Gandalf, orchestrate

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:18.950
an attack on Isengard, head to Mount Doom
in Mordor, destroy the One Ring, and fight

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:20.220
against the vicious Sauron.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:24.680
It's high fantasy at its finest, and you've
got a few days left to enjoy it on Netflix.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.080
Featuring one of the biggest twists in movie
history, The Sixth Sense centers around a

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.600
young boy named Cole Sear, who can see dead
people.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:36.100
Cole's troubled by his paranormal abilities,
which leads child psychologist Dr. Malcolm

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.480
Crowe to find the truth behind the boy's visions.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:43.360
In the end, they both get more than they bargained
for, and viewers get one unforgettable plot

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:43.860
twist.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:47.500
The Sixth Sense is available to stream on
Netflix until November 1.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:51.840
Have an extra three hours to spare and want
to spend it doing something meaningful?

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:57.380
Stream Richard Linklater's sprawling, deeply
intimate, Academy Award-nominated opus Boyhood.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:01.870
The film follows a boy named Mason Evans Jr.
as he comes of age in Texas alongside his

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.200
younger sister Samantha.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:08.340
Together with his divorced parents Olivia
and Mason Sr., Mason discovers facts of life,

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:10.180
and finds out what it means to be human.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.760
Linklater took an inventive approach with
Boyhood, shooting the film over the course

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:18.360
of 12 years from 2001 to 2013 with the exact
same cast.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:22.750
The end result is a touching depiction of
personal evolution as viewers watch Mason

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:24.720
literally grow up from year to year.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:28.580
Boyhood leaves Netflix a little later in the
month, on November 25.

